<title>NETHERLANDS: BREEVAST SETS 1996 STOCK DIV AT 1 PER 29.</title>
<headline>BREEVAST SETS 1996 STOCK DIV AT 1 PER 29.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property development firm Breevast NV said on Friday it had set its 1996 optional stock dividend at one new share per 29 held.</p>
<p>In March, it announced it would pay a 1996 cash dividend of 0.60 guilders, up from 0.50 in the previous year. The payment could be taken up in cash or as an alternative dividend in new shares.</p>
<p>Breevast shares closed at 15.90 guilders on the Amsterdam Stock Exchange on Friday, down 0.20 from their previous close.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 (fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
